[2]={["atomIDs"]={"2:description:1-122","2:description:125-242","2:objective:1-79"},["opening"]="Sharptalon's claw was a trophy destined for Senani Thunderheart at Splintertree Post. The hippogryph's remains could supply the evidence she needed for this part of the Ashenvale Hunt.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to bring Sharptalon's Claw to Senani.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Sharptalon's Claw to Senani Thunderheart.",["sourceHash"]="1156a12b5bd46c6de5fe1db5a30c2b104380d9427de11b14f8ff799d0638bd15",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[5]={["atomIDs"]={"5:description:1-102","5:description:220-314","5:objective:1-22"},["opening"]="Weeks of hiding in a ghost town had reduced Jitters to grubs and weeds. His hopes for a proper meal led to Chef Grual at Darkshire's Scarlet Raven Tavern, whose Dusky Crab Cakes had reached even this isolated refuge.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to ask Chef Grual about a meal for Jitters.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought Jitters' request to Chef Grual.",["sourceHash"]="ca90b596bee2ad106d5f3667c132f6933759382a07760345e0fd61b86fd75eb9",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[6]={["atomIDs"]={"6:description:1-173","6:description:176-224","6:description:229-244","6:description:247-294","6:description:297-332","6:objective:1-77"},["bridge"]="Garrick Padfoot's attacks had troubled Elwynn's farmers and merchants for weeks. Willem's latest report placed him beyond the bridge, near the vineyards east of the abbey, with a gang that made the bounty dangerous to pursue.",["bridgeFrom"]=18,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="Garrick Padfoot's attacks had troubled Elwynn's farmers and merchants for weeks. Willem's latest report placed him beyond the bridge, near the vineyards east of the abbey, with a gang that made the bounty dangerous to pursue.",["pending"]="{actor} would seek Padfoot and bring proof to Willem.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought Garrick Padfoot's head to Deputy Willem.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="6bc064d32b725f2b95e6cd1dd9f23fb8e21c2496d12e8b9a8f17da29fe37ce28",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7]={["aftermath"]="Even then, the marshal remained concerned about the danger that kobolds in large numbers posed to Stormwind.",["atomIDs"]={"7:description:1-40","7:description:43-97","7:description:100-145","7:description:148-218","7:objective:1-54"},["bridge"]="Kobolds had spread into the woods north of the abbey. McBride wanted their numbers reduced before Northshire could hope to drive the clan away altogether.",["bridgeFrom"]=783,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"7:completion:1-19","7:completion:21-105","7:completion:107-161","7:completion:166-207"},["opening"]="Kobolds had spread into the woods north of the abbey. McBride wanted their numbers reduced before Northshire could hope to drive the clan away altogether.",["pending"]="{actor} was to confront ten kobold vermin north of the abbey.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="McBride thanked {actor} for reducing the threat north of the abbey.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="730f34c2bae9f83a3f719c35da6df15614a973a1afc2a3e69a64fdf83351a924",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[8]={["atomIDs"]={"8:description:1-10","8:description:12-115","8:description:120-170","8:description:172-218","8:description:220-266","8:description:271-376","8:description:378-439","8:description:441-466","8:description:468-496","8:objective:1-69"},["opening"]="Calvin had a letter for an innkeeper in Brill. He described the tavern as a refuge for plague survivors finding their way again.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to carry Calvin's letter to Renee.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the letter to Renee.",["sourceHash"]="b7ce0e8a6d27adee4aefa4b40c76d988109fa98c99b8ad99fdfb300d90d8b29d",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[10]={["aftermath"]="Fizzledowser mourned Scrimshank and hoped the surveying records would give the loss meaning. His research suggested an outside controlling influence, but he still framed that force as a dangerous possibility.",["atomIDs"]={"10:description:1-26","10:description:29-119","10:description:122-161","10:description:164-250","10:description:253-322","10:description:327-399","10:description:402-408","10:description:410-450","10:description:453-504","10:objective:1-142"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"10:completion:1-39","10:completion:42-143","10:completion:148-228","10:completion:231-408","10:completion:411-494"},["opening"]="Scrimshank had disappeared after reporting more insects southeast of Gadgetzan. Fizzledowser feared the Gaping Chasm marked a second infestation and asked for his assistant, or at least the surveying equipment left behind.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to discover Scrimshank's fate and return him or his equipment.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the Scrimshank search and returned the required recovery to Fizzledowser.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="6f42d017d4c43e4e6b15e3b5573d895ca3bea867a7fdad1b190cc6cecbefaadd",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[11]={["atomIDs"]={"11:description:1-116","11:description:119-232","11:description:235-305","11:description:310-366","11:description:369-428","11:objective:1-64"},["bridge"]="The guards could not handle the Riverpaw packs along Elwynn's borders alone. Rainer described gatherings south of the tower and near Stone Cairn Lake; painted armbands would distinguish the campaign from an empty boast.",["bridgeFrom"]=239,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="The guards could not handle the Riverpaw packs along Elwynn's borders alone. Rainer described gatherings south of the tower and near Stone Cairn Lake; painted armbands would distinguish the campaign from an empty boast.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to gather eight painted gnoll armbands for Rainer.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the armbands to Deputy Rainer.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="60b84da9264d1e823061a3a4b840978224a7fa48131e977ffb64093643918b49",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[16]={["atomIDs"]={"16:requestItems:1-76","16:requestItems:81-130"},["coverageQualification"]="BASIC_RETAINED_EXCHANGE_CONTEXT",["minimumStage"]=3,["objectiveSummary"]="Bring refreshing spring water to Gerard Tiller.",["opening"]="Farming left Gerard thirsty. He offered a trade for refreshing spring water, making a small exchange part of the work around his fields.",["pending"]="{actor} would bring Gerard refreshing spring water.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} traded spring water with Gerard.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_SOURCE_REVIEWED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_CERTIFIED",["sourceHash"]="3eed088771b778ed5178fa7a8ffb0e5545da2412f5b079c4c198c65a2b7b37fe",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639",["unresolvedFields"]={"currentPlayability","unlistedQuantities"}},
[17]={["atomIDs"]={"17:description:1-73","17:description:76-199","17:description:202-278","17:description:283-338","17:description:341-402","17:description:407-495","17:objective:1-60"},["opening"]="Ghak wanted to study a newly discovered fungus for alchemy. Its clusters grew throughout Uldaman, but jostling them could release poisonous spores.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to gather twelve fungus caps.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the caps to Ghak.",["sourceHash"]="ce89051da206b7c5890b4c0e7710572c17d83f454827cea2a91e60c4055a4f0e",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[19]={["atomIDs"]={"19:description:1-89","19:description:92-165","19:description:168-199","19:objective:1-54"},["bridge"]="The danger included ambushes along the approach to Stonewatch. Marris singled out Tharil'zun, leader of the Blackrock Outrunners, for a separate strike.",["bridgeFrom"]=20,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="Ambushes lined the way to Stonewatch Keep. Marris singled out Tharil'zun, leader of the Blackrock Outrunners, and demanded his head.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to seek Tharil'zun's head for Marris.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought Tharil'zun's head to Marshal Marris.",["sourceHash"]="ce86264a823f491954fef6ceb0e5042afc9a26497146de83c3a6a70d9795f0af",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[20]={["atomIDs"]={"20:description:1-100","20:description:103-204","20:description:209-242","20:description:245-321","20:description:326-447","20:description:450-503","20:objective:1-56"},["opening"]="Blackrock orcs had occupied Stonewatch Keep after coming down from the Burning Steppes. Their raids penned Lakeshire's people inside the town, while further sightings reached Marris from southeastern Redridge. Ten battleworn axes would serve as proof for his campaign.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to gather ten Battleworn Axes for Marshal Marris.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered ten Battleworn Axes to Marshal Marris.",["sourceHash"]="6e4ebe91765f1e6daa10ec8d6ce3f8c46a9323efe40a1ac1fada8d508a82b43b",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[23]={["atomIDs"]={"23:description:1-88","23:description:91-186","23:description:191-349","23:objective:1-77"},["opening"]="A small quarter-crescent marked Ursangous's paw, its meaning unexplained. The trophy had to reach Senani at Splintertree Post to establish this part of the Ashenvale Hunt.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to take Ursangous's Paw to Senani.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Ursangous's Paw to Senani Thunderheart.",["sourceHash"]="c9eee9db19ac6a8194c8ed14b6b1fba14d36131ff6adfaecc3b697f259a7699f",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[24]={["atomIDs"]={"24:description:1-69","24:description:72-161","24:description:164-291","24:objective:1-78"},["opening"]="Shadumbra's head was the trophy named for another part of the Ashenvale Hunt. Senani Thunderheart at Splintertree Post was to receive it as proof.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to carry Shadumbra's Head to Senani.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Shadumbra's Head to Senani Thunderheart.",["sourceHash"]="8b11bd4c375aede7ff4edeca2cf46c864825d102db91fa589b47cfef0b371a13",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[25]={["atomIDs"]={"25:description:1-98","25:description:103-244","25:description:246-276","25:description:279-478","25:description:483-506","25:objective:1-121","25:objective:126-201","25:objective:206-264"},["opening"]="Befouled elementals in Mystral Lake had halted transport through Talondeep Path. Mastok also wanted the lake's gazebo scouted for its view of an Alliance outpost, joining a road problem to a military concern.",["pending"]="{actor} would confront twelve Befouled Water Elementals and scout the Mystral gazebo.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the elemental-and-gazebo assignment and returned to Mastok.",["sourceHash"]="0453200b67133f27b3d7f8bf8743b72dc760172de036b8d4135665da3f8402bf",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[32]={["aftermath"]="Zilzibin recognized the creatures as silithid. He warned that their role as tools of a greater power made the danger wider than Tanaris or one faction.",["atomIDs"]={"32:description:1-19","32:description:22-109","32:description:114-163","32:description:166-278","32:description:281-391","32:description:394-437","32:description:442-506","32:objective:1-50"},["bridge"]="The analysis report had returned to Fizzledowser. He sent a copy to Zilzibin Drumlore, seeking knowledge that the surveyors' work alone could not supply.",["bridgeFrom"]=113,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"32:completion:1-14","32:completion:16-51","32:completion:53-87","32:completion:89-103","32:completion:108-240","32:completion:242-291","32:completion:293-429","32:completion:434-481"},["opening"]="Fizzledowser sent the insect report beyond Gadgetzan to Zilzibin Drumlore. The Orgrimmar scholar's studies of unusual life and history might explain a threat the surveyors could no longer address alone.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to deliver the report to Zilzibin Drumlore.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the report to Zilzibin Drumlore in Orgrimmar.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="4576f238d321b1c485b227eeea1449f549a4df4ad87077696a8dfd14daf7d3b8",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[34]={["atomIDs"]={"34:description:1-47","34:description:89-167","34:description:172-235","34:description:312-359","34:description:362-488","34:objective:1-57","34:objective:60-87"},["opening"]="Bellygrub had trampled Martie Jainrose's garden again. The boar foraged southwest of Lakeshire and sometimes wandered into her flowers; Martie wanted his tusk as proof that the raids had ended.",["pending"]="{actor} would deal with Bellygrub and bring his tusk to Martie.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} fulfilled Martie's assignment against Bellygrub and delivered his tusk.",["sourceHash"]="f1bc27b7bb41d85bd59f74a36e66baba7d6973f7d984df99a745439153bcbce8",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[35]={["aftermath"]="Thomas confirmed that aggressive murlocs had settled beside the eastern streams, though their reason for coming remained unknown.",["atomIDs"]={"35:description:1-138","35:description:141-230","35:description:235-254","35:objective:1-52"},["bridge"]="Dughan's doubts led east to the bridge. Guard Thomas had spent the past week stationed there and could provide the firsthand military account the marshal needed.",["bridgeFrom"]=40,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"35:completion:1-70","35:completion:72-158"},["opening"]="Dughan's doubts led east to the bridge. Guard Thomas had spent the past week stationed there and could provide the firsthand military account the marshal needed.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to ask Guard Thomas about conditions at the bridge.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} consulted Guard Thomas in eastern Elwynn.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="ef045029a938d9921daaae837bfbcc0347c280d6ef5f166c235d7961e180bf2f",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[37]={["aftermath"]="A medallion identified the stripped corpse as Footman Malakai Stone.",["atomIDs"]={"37:description:1-116","37:description:119-180","37:description:185-235","37:description:237-253","37:objective:1-105"},["bridge"]="Thomas's report lacked the fate of two men. Rolf and Malakai had gone upriver to investigate days earlier and never returned; the search now had to allow for the possibility of finding only their remains.",["bridgeFrom"]=35,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"37:completion:1-133"},["opening"]="Thomas's report lacked the fate of two men. Rolf and Malakai had gone upriver to investigate days earlier and never returned; the search now had to allow for the possibility of finding only their remains.",["pending"]="{actor} would search north along the river for the missing guards.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the first search for Rolf and Malakai.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="d0a9dfc56711b6dc547993366dda1b26d0be847b54eab017f9cef74ccdfcd67c",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[39]={["aftermath"]="Dughan feared the fighting might reach Goldshire if the situation did not improve; it was a warning, not news of an attack already begun.",["atomIDs"]={"39:description:1-153","39:description:158-238","39:objective:1-38"},["bridge"]="Thomas's warning was now a military report: Rolf and Malakai were dead, and the troops in eastern Elwynn could not contain the murlocs. Dughan had to hear how thin the defense had become.",["bridgeFrom"]=71,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"39:completion:1-28","39:completion:30-148","39:completion:153-231"},["opening"]="Thomas's warning was now a military report: Rolf and Malakai were dead, and the troops in eastern Elwynn could not contain the murlocs. Dughan had to hear how thin the defense had become.",["pending"]="{actor} was to carry Thomas's report back to Goldshire.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reported the guards' deaths and the eastern threat to Dughan.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="b0fa8b9f320acfe307a7e0a77eb35d1c804e9f7f6c2945f5bc9a4622e1a3196a",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[40]={["aftermath"]="Dughan wanted a military report before moving troops. He respected Remy, but considered the reports uncertain.",["atomIDs"]={"40:description:1-42","40:description:45-143","40:description:148-227","40:description:230-278","40:description:283-359","40:objective:1-69"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"40:completion:1-23","40:completion:25-121","40:completion:126-250"},["opening"]="Remy had seen murlocs coming upstream into eastern Elwynn, frightening away fish and attacking travelers. Dughan remained occupied with gnolls and bandits; a merchant's warning had not persuaded him to spare more troops.",["pending"]="{actor} would take Remy's warning to Marshal Dughan.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} raised the eastern murloc threat with Dughan.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="f5295cb5c6126d2c3e426d083a8f5418a5f87b812b8c100ddf3a920406210708",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[45]={["aftermath"]="The corpse's medallion bore the name Footman Rolf Hartford.",["atomIDs"]={"45:description:1-109","45:description:112-181","45:description:186-219","45:objective:1-58"},["bridge"]="Webbed tracks continued east along Stone Cairn Lake toward a murloc village. They offered a grim direction for the search for Rolf, without yet establishing where it would end.",["bridgeFrom"]=37,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"45:completion:1-106"},["opening"]="Webbed tracks continued east along Stone Cairn Lake toward a murloc village. They offered a grim direction for the search for Rolf, without yet establishing where it would end.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to search the village for Rolf or evidence of his fate.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the search for Rolf at the lakeside village.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="fd4d12750b23638e88fd7373764a666eeb04c853ab5e185bffeeb6430bcc3119",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[48]={["atomIDs"]={"48:description:1-52","48:description:55-98","48:description:101-135","48:description:138-176","48:objective:1-49"},["opening"]="Grimbooze Thunderbrew's recipe began with a riddle. To the south, among twisting vines, a hidden well held the spring water he wanted for his amber brew.",["pending"]="{actor} would bring Holy Spring Water to Grimbooze.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied the spring water for Grimbooze's brew.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="fa5f5723cfc5e78b971a059f04c5b41b8bb3b372aca55e8c4663bdaa1dba427a",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[49]={["atomIDs"]={"49:description:1-42","49:description:45-89","49:description:92-136","49:description:139-177","49:objective:1-79"},["bridge"]="Water alone would not make Grimbooze's long-imagined drink. The next part of his recipe called for three grains: barley, rye and corn, each carried in its own sack.",["bridgeFrom"]=48,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="Water alone would not make Grimbooze's long-imagined drink. The next part of his recipe called for three grains: barley, rye and corn, each carried in its own sack.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to bring the three sacks of grain to Grimbooze.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied Grimbooze with barley, rye and corn.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="8b7aaa0789b7791d89bfad051d03e64567c74749bd2f5fc10c92191cc0a3dc98",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
