[51]={["atomIDs"]={"51:description:1-38","51:description:41-80","51:description:83-122","51:description:125-174","51:objective:1-49"},["bridge"]="Fresh distillation was only another stage in Grimbooze's recipe. Before the liquid could be filtered, he needed a sycamore branch for the charcoal.",["bridgeFrom"]=50,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="Fresh distillation was only another stage in Grimbooze's recipe. Before the liquid could be filtered, he needed a sycamore branch for the charcoal.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to bring Grimbooze a sycamore branch.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied the branch for the brewer's charcoal.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="a9caffecbac956f91ea9453617f6b52b2a24bc94ad208f4bed2d1c8a85289c15",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[53]={["aftermath"]="Grimbooze celebrated the completed recipe by proposing a toast.",["atomIDs"]={"53:description:1-42","53:description:45-84","53:description:87-130","53:description:133-170","53:objective:1-52"},["bridge"]="Grimbooze still needed a barrel in which the clear spirit could age toward amber. Charred oak would complete the vessel; the drink's color belonged to the years of maturation he described, not to an instant transformation.",["bridgeFrom"]=51,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"53:completion:1-41","53:completion:44-91","53:completion:94-129","53:completion:132-179"},["opening"]="Grimbooze still needed a barrel in which the clear spirit could age toward amber. Charred oak would complete the vessel; the drink's color belonged to the years of maturation he described, not to an instant transformation.",["pending"]="{actor} would find charred oak for Grimbooze's barrel.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the charred oak to Grimbooze.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="21cf139ca077276c064574ec5d3be47b2bd0110cb409ca825cbbe3d80ed9e6de",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[55]={["aftermath"]="Sven acknowledged Morbent Fel's defeat while the Dark Riders remained beyond his reach. One part of his revenge had an answer; the wider pursuit did not.",["atomIDs"]={"55:description:1-111","55:description:163-193","55:description:196-242","55:description:247-255","55:description:258-299","55:description:302-357","55:objective:1-100"},["bridge"]="Morbent's Bane had reached Sven. He directed its use against the necromancer's protections at the house overlooking Raven Hill cemetery, where preparation would have to become confrontation.",["bridgeFrom"]=325,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"55:completion:1-30","55:completion:32-140","55:completion:145-234","55:completion:247-300"},["opening"]="Morbent Fel kept his lair in the house above Raven Hill cemetery. Sven sent Morbent's Bane to strip the necromancer's protections before the confrontation, binding his demand for revenge to Duskwood's need for relief.",["pending"]="{actor} would use Morbent's Bane against Morbent Fel and return the weapon to Sven after the assignment.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the assignment against Morbent Fel and returned Morbent's Bane to Sven.",["sourceHash"]="45c79219ec369b1a4ea61280efd32b84fb25c2d46664ce62ff202ca6675b34a2",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[56]={["atomIDs"]={"56:description:1-89","56:description:92-194","56:description:250-392","56:objective:1-99"},["opening"]="Stormwind had withdrawn its commissioned guards, leaving Darkshire's defense to the Night Watch. Commander Althea Ebonlocke needed help against the skeletal warriors and mages gathering in Tranquil Gardens, just south of town.",["pending"]="{actor} would meet the Night Watch's assignment against eight Skeletal Warriors and six Skeletal Mages.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} fulfilled Ebonlocke's assignment against the warriors and mages.",["sourceHash"]="59f75d213ea4a884962af47d85c5d0152e2722dfb377a08546d1c7ee5d9109a6",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[57]={["atomIDs"]={"57:description:1-63","57:description:66-192","57:description:195-295","57:objective:1-101"},["bridge"]="The assignment at Tranquil Gardens had not exhausted the Night Watch's need. Ebonlocke now had reports of fiends and horrors at Raven Hill as well as the southern cemetery, and called for fifteen of each.",["bridgeFrom"]=56,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="Reports of skeletons reached Ebonlocke from both Raven Hill and the cemetery south of Darkshire. The Watch's work extended beyond a single burial ground; its next assignment called for fifteen Skeletal Fiends and fifteen Skeletal Horrors.",["pending"]="{actor} would answer the reports by confronting the specified fiends and horrors.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the Watch's assignment against fifteen Skeletal Fiends and fifteen Skeletal Horrors.",["sourceHash"]="bbf09a4e5b8e933b704bbcf8332e8cf76dd08d427295049a8ca5e946680f957a",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[58]={["atomIDs"]={"58:description:1-42","58:description:92-142","58:description:145-246","58:objective:1-114"},["bridge"]="The reports from the graveyards led to a more concentrated danger. Raven Hill's eastern mausoleum still held Plague Spreaders, and Ebonlocke lacked the Watchers to spare; twenty became the next assignment.",["bridgeFrom"]=57,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="The eastern mausoleum at Raven Hill remained a danger to Darkshire. Ebonlocke lacked enough Watchers to secure the town and called for twenty Plague Spreaders to be removed from the mausoleum.",["pending"]="{actor} would undertake the assignment against twenty Plague Spreaders.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} fulfilled the eastern mausoleum assignment for the Night Watch.",["sourceHash"]="6a682c0e4e29b230aaf08a2a787f92a51894d13eb8617a22c3c92c35b342a5fa",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[59]={["aftermath"]="Sara offered a choice of armor for Elwynn's defense.",["atomIDs"]={"59:description:1-88","59:description:91-160","59:description:163-222","59:description:225-286","59:description:291-357","59:objective:1-48"},["bridge"]="Dughan offered an armor marker in recognition of service to Elwynn. Sara Timberlain at Eastvale Logging Camp could honor it, beyond Thomas's post to the east.",["bridgeFrom"]=39,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"59:completion:1-29","59:completion:31-76","59:completion:81-102","59:completion:104-137"},["opening"]="Dughan offered an armor marker in recognition of service to Elwynn. Sara Timberlain at Eastvale Logging Camp could honor it, beyond Thomas's post to the east.",["pending"]="{actor} would take the Stormwind armor marker to Sara Timberlain.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} presented the marker to Sara Timberlain.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="ef9fde6e26df99e59b262f94818f449f34cbafa19849ba3df9ae44229fa45207",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[63]={["atomIDs"]={"63:description:1-115","63:description:117-238","63:description:243-352","63:description:354-433","63:description:438-508","63:objective:1-186"},["opening"]="Silverpine's plague had tainted the coastal shrine and silenced its spirits. Islen prescribed a confrontation with the corrupted manifestation, then an offering of its bracers and the remaining pure water at Everfount's brazier.",["pending"]="{actor} would confront the Corrupt Manifestation of Water and make the prescribed brazier offering.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the manifestation-and-brazier assignment in Silverpine Forest.",["sourceClassMask"]="64",["sourceHash"]="617e736899d433c51367fbb4c0d2eb68680a6ab12c3965d6c4ccac39c38f754e",["sourceMapID"]="?",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[66]={["atomIDs"]={"66:description:1-59","66:description:62-121","66:description:124-186","66:description:191-296","66:description:299-337","66:description:342-431","66:objective:1-53"},["opening"]="Madame Eva feared for her granddaughter Alyssa. A disturbing premonition and a reading of the cards had yielded only the name Stalvan; Darkshire's town registry might turn that fearful impression into a lead.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to ask Clerk Daltry about Stalvan.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} carried Madame Eva's inquiry to Clerk Daltry.",["sourceHash"]="ac82b5b671db17cc1441ad56a4d7d28d3ac7fa52c9eeb401abeadda76eba5d99",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[67]={["atomIDs"]={"67:description:128-146","67:description:149-203","67:description:206-229","67:description:234-264","67:description:356-388","67:objective:1-105"},["opening"]="Daltry's registry placed Stalvan Mistmantle at the Moonbrook Schoolhouse, but the address was plainly old. The clerk wanted newer information, making the abandoned record the starting point for a search in Westfall.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to search the Moonbrook Schoolhouse for information about Stalvan.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the schoolhouse inquiry into Stalvan.",["sourceHash"]="d8b7a981bbecfccc0f88ca46b4abb333b80a43f8f6d9daba3b1ac0fe2d9a1a3c",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[68]={["atomIDs"]={"68:description:1-53","68:objective:1-45"},["opening"]="A dusty letter lay unsent in the schoolhouse footlocker. The document could give Daltry more than the stale address recorded beside Stalvan's name.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to take the Dusty Unsent Letter to Daltry.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Dusty Unsent Letter to the Darkshire clerk.",["sourceHash"]="8ed9733508a052af6d517bc0337f45de1681742de9fca601cef888f53706210a",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[69]={["atomIDs"]={"69:description:48-165","69:description:168-234","69:description:237-266","69:objective:1-80"},["bridge"]="The unsent letter had returned the search to Daltry's records. A second, half-erased address beneath the first entry pointed beyond Moonbrook to the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire.",["bridgeFrom"]=68,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="A second address had emerged beneath the first entry in the registry, partly scratched out. It pointed toward the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, where someone might still remember Stalvan.",["pending"]="{actor} would inquire about Stalvan at the Lion's Pride Inn.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought the inquiry to Innkeeper Farley at the Lion's Pride.",["sourceHash"]="8f0bd462973f5b13d34642345aa44239d1d2a23f3f2856f4c06596e895636535",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[70]={["atomIDs"]={"70:description:52-137","70:description:140-231","70:description:234-296","70:description:301-357","70:description:360-386","70:description:388-470","70:objective:1-103"},["opening"]="Farley remembered a messenger who fled the inn in terror on a stormy night, leaving his letters behind. One letter from Stalvan still waited upstairs, addressed to Stormwind's Canal District.",["pending"]="{actor} would retrieve Stalvan's Undelivered Letter and carry it to the Canal District.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Stalvan's Undelivered Letter to Caretaker Folsom.",["sourceHash"]="ef8baf1292f0f73de5eb8625ad126700b8996c6665cbe3477ce8bf474133fced",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[71]={["aftermath"]="Thomas accepted that the murloc threat could no longer be ignored.",["atomIDs"]={"71:description:1-132","71:objective:1-83"},["bridge"]="The two medallions were evidence Thomas needed, however unwelcome the answer. They would give the guard at the bridge a definite account of what had happened to Rolf and Malakai.",["bridgeFrom"]=45,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"71:completion:1-32","71:completion:34-75"},["opening"]="The two medallions were evidence Thomas needed, however unwelcome the answer. They would give the guard at the bridge a definite account of what had happened to Rolf and Malakai.",["pending"]="{actor} would carry both medallions to Guard Thomas.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Rolf's and Malakai's medallions to Thomas.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="da5213d54c1e9de1064232f94f3dd76d3c6c58b3da7865b1d3d3a7aad74299a1",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[72]={["atomIDs"]={"72:description:1-60","72:description:63-108","72:description:149-201","72:description:204-265","72:description:293-377","72:objective:1-52"},["opening"]="Folsom's father once cleaned the estate after a massacre. Now the Flintridge trust had run dry, and the family's remaining possessions were packed for auction. Folsom permitted a search through those remnants for another clue.",["pending"]="{actor} would examine the packed possessions for a lead.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the search among the estate's packed possessions.",["sourceHash"]="63fa49a013e1eaed1144c50a38ae288366990ab87d7a6e66dea098b70f0608e9",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[74]={["atomIDs"]={"74:description:1-121","74:description:124-199","74:objective:1-61"},["factSourceMetadata"]={"finisherName","finisherIDs"},["opening"]="Among the estate's heirlooms, books and hunting trophies, a torn journal page had surfaced beneath a vase. The fragment offered the next lead in the search for Stalvan.",["pending"]="{actor} would follow the clue provided by the Torn Journal Page.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} presented the Torn Journal Page to Marshal Haggard.",["sourceHash"]="6aa0988490c799cb0167d204bdb5b32947d1b3c6411be917d91104bbed27e1f0",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[75]={["atomIDs"]={"75:description:1-84","75:description:87-178","75:description:184-341","75:description:344-421","75:description:424-468","75:objective:1-81"},["opening"]="Haggard remembered papers left in an upstairs chest when he moved in. His failing sight kept him from reading them, but a faded journal page might connect those old papers with the inquiry into Stalvan.",["pending"]="{actor} would look in Haggard's upstairs chest for the Faded Journal Page.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought the Faded Journal Page to Marshal Haggard.",["sourceHash"]="0f2901b79b670d41b387dad4d7f34c217b0459863823855148e101f093340773",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[77]={["aftermath"]="Gilveradin admitted that ordinary empty packaging, rather than magic, would accomplish the deception.",["atomIDs"]={"77:description:1-74","77:description:77-149","77:description:151-201","77:description:204-280","77:description:285-433","77:description:436-502","77:objective:1-117"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"77:completion:1-20","77:completion:22-97","77:completion:99-187","77:completion:192-266","77:completion:268-363","77:completion:365-442","77:completion:447-471"},["opening"]="Gilveradin had the original packing for the sought honey ripple and offered to disguise recovered bottles as the old treasure. His fee required extra bottles from an abandoned Horde base now occupied by oozes.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to recover ten bottles for packaging.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought the ripple to Gilveradin.",["sourceHash"]="06fc4a010c8f0e88e0b453f2698325918ef980cd9fa6f5130953d919a51ca34b",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[78]={["atomIDs"]={"78:description:53-160","78:description:163-229","78:description:232-286","78:objective:1-49"},["bridge"]="The faded page had emerged from Haggard's upstairs chest, but its meaning required another reader. Haggard remembered Smitts' command of local lore from his own days with the Stormwind Guard and sent the fragment back to Darkshire.",["bridgeFrom"]=75,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="Haggard's memory led back to the Scarlet Raven Tavern. Its keeper, Smitts, knew the local lore when Haggard served with the Stormwind Guard and might recognize what the faded page preserved.",["pending"]="{actor} would show the Faded Journal Page to Tavernkeep Smitts.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Faded Journal Page to Smitts.",["sourceHash"]="344a922d7ca850b21ad7669929b84710c7c530d3f2ceb18454911b719b1e550a",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[79]={["atomIDs"]={"79:description:1-58","79:description:61-156","79:description:159-262","79:description:265-304","79:description:307-393","79:objective:1-43"},["opening"]="Smitts recalled investigating the slaughter of visiting nobles with Haggard. Muddy pages found then could never be linked to Stalvan; he believed the new evidence supplied that link and sent it urgently to Darkshire's commander.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to carry Smitts' muddy page and findings to Commander Ebonlocke.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} placed the muddy page before Commander Ebonlocke.",["sourceHash"]="28ca7b7918cca0a5147b0582a1f50642574d7fd5bc85b695fcd3e573e2c22700",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[80]={["aftermath"]="Daltry confirmed that the journal page and the registry signatures shared the same handwriting. The comparison supplied the link Ebonlocke had required.",["atomIDs"]={"80:description:64-156","80:description:161-264","80:description:267-347","80:objective:1-48"},["bridge"]="Smitts' evidence had reached Darkshire's commander. Ebonlocke still wanted the handwriting compared with the town registry, leaving Daltry to test the connection before suspicion became a settled case.",["bridgeFrom"]=79,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"80:completion:1-8","80:completion:10-85"},["opening"]="Ebonlocke wanted the handwriting tested before the case was settled. Daltry's years with the town registry made him the person to compare the bloodstained page with Stalvan's recorded signature.",["pending"]="{actor} would show Daltry the Bloodstained Journal Page for comparison.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} submitted the Bloodstained Journal Page to Clerk Daltry.",["sourceHash"]="663d2730a848352767155d58213b7e341b011f4205fc483740cdb40756c08cb9",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[81]={["aftermath"]="Dran confirmed the contents and anticipated profit from the tavern sale while keeping extra bottles for himself.",["atomIDs"]={"81:description:1-141","81:description:144-225","81:description:228-242","81:description:247-324","81:description:327-504","81:objective:1-49"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"81:completion:1-38","81:completion:43-86","81:completion:88-137","81:completion:139-203","81:completion:205-212","81:completion:217-307","81:completion:309-347","81:completion:349-363","81:completion:365-375"},["opening"]="Gilveradin packed the salvage and extra bottles carefully despite his low opinion of Dran. The barrel now joined a commercial delivery to greetings for an old drinking companion.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to bring the secured barrel to Dran.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the ripple to Orgrimmar.",["sourceHash"]="f4fa7e8b520392a7162aa5326563e8b5169ca39999714e99f703ce2fa66a0eca",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[82]={["aftermath"]="Pestlezugg found the parts unlike insect forms he knew and suspected an outside controlling force. Before analysis was complete, another urgent report required Fizzledowser's attention.",["atomIDs"]={"82:description:1-46","82:description:48-144","82:description:146-190","82:description:195-234","82:description:236-317","82:description:319-412","82:description:414-466","82:objective:1-93"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"82:completion:1-48","82:completion:50-94","82:completion:96-151","82:completion:153-235","82:completion:240-363","82:completion:365-441"},["opening"]="Insects had drained the Noxious Lair's former pools, but the surveyors knew little else about them. Fizzledowser requested five Centipaar parts for Pestlezugg to examine before plans were made against an unknown enemy.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to recover five Centipaar insect parts for Pestlezugg.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered five Centipaar insect parts to Alchemist Pestlezugg.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="a9b7eea8fdba0e6af6d09dc0260486e73e166156a164a44c1e8c759e9afcc0d9",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[84]={["aftermath"]="With the pie before him, Billy said his memory was returning.",["atomIDs"]={"84:description:1-12","84:description:15-92","84:objective:1-67"},["bridge"]="Bernice had made the pie, though her anger toward Billy had hardly softened. Carrying it back to the Maclure vineyards was the price of hearing what the boy remembered about her missing necklace.",["bridgeFrom"]=86,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"84:completion:1-8","84:completion:10-30","84:completion:35-75"},["opening"]="Bernice had made the pie, though her anger toward Billy had hardly softened. Carrying it back to the Maclure vineyards was the price of hearing what the boy remembered about her missing necklace.",["pending"]="{actor} would take the pork belly pie to Billy Maclure.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Bernice's pie to Billy.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="8b1d457505c58d6c3b96fd335694709eae90d2a1e3565c68523685d7e3ac98eb",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[87]={["aftermath"]="Bernice remembered her husband's luck and his last campaign when offering thanks for the necklace's return.",["atomIDs"]={"87:description:1-105","87:description:108-152","87:description:157-248","87:description:251-308","87:objective:1-79"},["bridge"]="Billy's story shifted around the Fargodeep Mine. He denied responsibility for the necklace, but said a large gold-toothed kobold had picked it up and carried it inside. Bernice's missing property now had a lead.",["bridgeFrom"]=84,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"87:completion:1-17","87:completion:19-44","87:completion:49-64","87:completion:66-117","87:completion:119-167","87:completion:169-175"},["opening"]="Billy's story shifted around the Fargodeep Mine. He denied responsibility for the necklace, but said a large gold-toothed kobold had picked it up and carried it inside. Bernice's missing property now had a lead.",["pending"]="{actor} would search for Goldtooth and recover Bernice's necklace.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned the necklace to Bernice Stonefield.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="6dbf979583a7a30b7ed5bef0f3a43b63f7cd49bbcf16ca1adaf7bc924089945e",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[89]={["atomIDs"]={"89:description:1-101","89:description:104-256","89:description:261-325","89:description:328-414","89:description:420-441","89:objective:1-67"},["opening"]="Iron went into weapons during the last invasion, and gnolls stole the replacement shipment from Stormwind. Oslow needed pikes and rivets from the stolen supplies to continue rebuilding Lakeshire's bridge.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to recover five Iron Pikes and five Iron Rivets for Oslow.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied Oslow with five Iron Pikes and five Iron Rivets for the bridge work.",["sourceHash"]="396469655bdb9f02d6e100782f1802d25dfbc6bd2ee30b3ebeefc9111ff97e75",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[90]={["atomIDs"]={"90:description:1-42","90:description:45-70","90:description:73-105","90:description:108-178","90:description:181-273","90:description:276-359","90:objective:1-95"},["opening"]="Grual's wolf kabobs required more than meat from Duskwood. Ten lean flanks had to be joined by seasoning herbs from Felicia Gump's flower shop in Stormwind's Canal District.",["pending"]="{actor} would obtain the wolf flanks and Stormwind Seasoning Herbs for Grual.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered ten Lean Wolf Flanks and the seasoning herbs to Chef Grual.",["sourceHash"]="d54cc8c46f1e53d1c5b5190aa2031878ad4bb46fce8aa4acf90514650f868562",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[91]={["atomIDs"]={"91:description:1-82","91:description:84-176","91:description:178-233","91:description:238-309","91:description:311-401","91:description:406-438","91:description:443-506","91:objective:1-76"},["opening"]="Conacher accused Morganth of terrorizing Lakeshire through the Shadowhide gnolls. Under the town's law, aiding an enemy of the kingdom carried a death sentence; the bailiff called for ten pendants as proof of enforcement.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to bring ten Shadowhide Pendants to Bailiff Conacher.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered ten Shadowhide Pendants to Bailiff Conacher.",["sourceHash"]="b9c8b5d1cd532609e36471f3f4cd0ab8153c15a01060bf9c8e3e0416adf41e60",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[92]={["atomIDs"]={"92:description:1-68","92:description:70-98","92:description:100-175","92:description:177-200","92:description:202-272","92:description:277-390","92:objective:1-132"},["opening"]="Feeding Stormwind's brigade during the uprising emptied Breanna's cupboard. She could make Redridge Goulash again if supplied with condor meat, goretusk snouts and crisp spider meat.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to gather five portions of each ingredient for Breanna's goulash.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied Breanna with five Tough Condor Meats, five Great Goretusk Snouts and five Crisp Spider Meats.",["sourceHash"]="ae69fc807b8cb65f94e69b74f9ec5f57717275022144d74bdd073a87a86c2df7",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[93]={["atomIDs"]={"93:description:1-89","93:description:186-247","93:description:252-356","93:objective:1-69"},["bridge"]="Jitters' hunger had led to Darkshire's kitchen, where the name of Grual's specialty concealed its ingredients. The cook needed six Gooey Spider Legs from the forest to prepare the promised crab cakes.",["bridgeFrom"]=5,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="The promised crab cakes concealed a local expedient: Grual cooked them with spider legs. Venom Web Spiders north of Darkshire could supply the six legs he needed, turning one of Duskwood's hazards into food for a hungry man.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to gather six Gooey Spider Legs for Grual.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied Grual with the six spider legs for his cakes.",["sourceHash"]="68af821c1659d3e4f9eed07a93745b8b4f9df8e6becff09ec8faa304d0d8e8dd",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[94]={["atomIDs"]={"94:description:1-99","94:description:102-193","94:description:198-226","94:description:228-249","94:description:254-325","94:description:328-372","94:description:377-460","94:objective:1-81"},["opening"]="Theocritus could watch his rival Morganth through the Eye of Azora, but wanted to see further into the mage's plans. A glyph placed on the lion statue near Redridge's Tower of Ilgalar was intended to extend that surveillance.",["pending"]="{actor} would place the Glyph of Azora on the lion statue near Ilgalar.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought the Glyph of Azora to the lion statue near Ilgalar.",["sourceHash"]="4d71889f9c4c99d6c7aa6fac59e944e533be455e84eaabe5b06b7fb651bdcc74",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[95]={["atomIDs"]={"95:description:1-153","95:description:158-237","95:description:240-341","95:description:344-381","95:description:386-454","95:description:457-509","95:objective:1-64"},["opening"]="Sven Yorgen said Dark Riders killed his family while he was away. On returning to the farm, he saw a shadowy stranger bury something near the barn. His pursuit of the riders left that hidden object unexplored.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to search behind the old stump at Sven's farm.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} located the burial place behind the old stump.",["sourceHash"]="3b83bacc9d57e01a7f72520b6e29c35b9893a89b10a46196ce34a90ad7b5a161",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[96]={["atomIDs"]={"96:description:1-11","96:description:13-37","96:description:42-66","96:description:68-94","96:description:96-117","96:description:122-166","96:objective:1-59"},["opening"]="The pure water spirit offered a shard with a lesson: water sustained life where corruption stopped it. The shard was to return to Islen as the tangible part of that understanding.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to bring the Shard of Water to Islen.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Shard of Water to Islen Waterseer.",["sourceClassMask"]="64",["sourceHash"]="4149a7e16cabd3595cd98ede5ae7927131363f173d2dec177e8371cbb71bf27e",["sourceMapID"]="?",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[97]={["atomIDs"]={"97:description:1-74","97:description:77-104","97:objective:1-39"},["bridge"]="Daltry's comparison had supplied the missing match. The next journey crossed no distant country: the finding simply needed to return to Ebonlocke before the inquiry could move beyond paper.",["bridgeFrom"]=80,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="Daltry had matched the handwriting on the page to the registry. That finding had to return to Ebonlocke, turning the paper trail into information Darkshire's commander could act upon.",["pending"]="{actor} would report the handwriting match to Ebonlocke.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reported Daltry's finding to Commander Ebonlocke.",["sourceHash"]="6d0021afb9b2d7d173fc5aad6dd2bf271080159ad59c1ab415f4eb33fa897b40",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[98]={["aftermath"]="Madame Eva understood that Stalvan was dead. Relief at the end of his threat was tempered, in her account, by remembrance of those he had already killed.",["atomIDs"]={"98:description:1-43","98:description:46-79","98:description:129-164","98:description:222-305","98:description:310-384","98:description:387-456","98:objective:1-60"},["bridge"]="The handwriting match had returned to Ebonlocke. She now ordered the confrontation at Stalvan's northern cottage, with his family ring destined for Madame Eva, whose fear for Alyssa had first given the inquiry its name.",["bridgeFrom"]=97,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"98:completion:1-28","98:completion:30-87","98:completion:89-145","98:completion:147-222","98:completion:224-267"},["opening"]="Ebonlocke now held Stalvan Mistmantle responsible for innocent deaths and feared further violence against Darkshire. She ordered his execution at the cottage north of town, with his family ring to go to Madame Eva, whose warning began the inquiry.",["pending"]="{actor} would confront Stalvan and bring his family ring to Madame Eva.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the assignment against Stalvan and presented his family ring to Madame Eva.",["sourceHash"]="36e6701e457e8059626599b68ca1a87141d86104d92b5fea2181f34333168855",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[99]={["aftermath"]="Dalar considered the gathered knowledge a means to oppose Arugal; undoing the curse remained his aim.",["atomIDs"]={"99:description:1-84","99:description:87-147","99:description:152-272","99:description:275-314","99:description:317-383","99:description:388-457","99:description:460-507","99:objective:1-63"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"99:completion:1-32","99:completion:34-130","99:completion:132-149"},["opening"]="Dalar's inquiry had reached Pyrewood, where villagers appeared human by day and became worgen at night. He sought the enchantment in their shackles to complete his research.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to gather six Pyrewood shackles.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied Dalar with the Pyrewood shackles.",["sourceHash"]="0a4181e9754cccb5c3c0abe6b4f908b62b7eee206c225cda68f4a02d5e7acc1d",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[100]={["atomIDs"]={"100:description:1-45","100:description:47-186","100:objective:1-63"},["opening"]="The incantation ended in light as water struck the flame and the corrupt spirits were destroyed. A pure manifestation remained to be addressed at the Silverpine shrine.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to speak with the Minor Manifestation of Water.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with the Minor Manifestation of Water in Silverpine Forest.",["sourceClassMask"]="64",["sourceHash"]="874ea172c46a6cdace820de104962a16fcb876cacce871d195511cbea8fbdcef",["sourceMapID"]="?",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[101]={["atomIDs"]={"101:description:1-96","101:description:99-204","101:description:209-327","101:description:330-434","101:objective:1-97"},["opening"]="Madame Eva read danger in the spreading taint of Duskwood. She offered a protective totem, but its enchantment required the forest's own grim materials: ghoul fangs, skeleton fingers and spider venom.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to gather the fangs, fingers and venom Madame Eva requests.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered ten Ghoul Fangs, ten Skeleton Fingers and five Vials of Spider Venom to Madame Eva.",["sourceHash"]="76a985df4b9476f10e84cc94969a7634b79ce4f1ab89296563dd3d742eccf081",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[102]={["aftermath"]="Danuvin hoped that aid to the militia might help Westfall become prosperous again. That future remained a hope.",["atomIDs"]={"102:description:1-27","102:description:30-93","102:description:96-186","102:description:189-233","102:description:238-317","102:description:320-421","102:description:423-479","102:objective:1-55"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"102:completion:1-14","102:completion:16-167","102:completion:169-227"},["opening"]="Danuvin would not abandon Westfall's remaining citizens, even if Stormwind had forgotten them. The former farmers of the People's Militia faced gnolls he believed were working with the Deadmines thieves.",["pending"]="{actor} would patrol Westfall and bring Danuvin eight gnoll paws.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the gnoll paws to Captain Danuvin.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="5db56372c392f760db3d41d9989f91567f1f560efeebb28f939cc1c15a6db48b",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[103]={["aftermath"]="Grayson saw the burning light as protection against the needless deaths that had marked his own afterlife.",["atomIDs"]={"103:description:1-59","103:description:62-113","103:description:116-269","103:description:272-348","103:description:353-436","103:objective:1-68"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"103:completion:1-21","103:completion:23-92","103:completion:94-152","103:completion:157-193","103:completion:195-257"},["opening"]="The lighthouse needed fuel even after its keeper's family was gone. Captain Grayson's vigil concerned sailors still approaching the dangerous rocks; oil from the harvest machines could keep the warning flame alive.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to bring five flasks of oil to the lighthouse.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied Captain Grayson with the oil.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="5e026671cb91345423bea194b5a775ab384a2e3192e5b1c6044f1828889b712b",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[104]={["aftermath"]="Grayson regarded Murk-Eye's death as a measure of safety for the coast, not an end to every peril of the Great Sea.",["atomIDs"]={"104:description:1-84","104:description:87-178","104:description:181-309","104:description:312-399","104:description:404-506","104:objective:1-76"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"104:completion:1-38","104:completion:40-53","104:completion:55-127","104:completion:129-232"},["opening"]="Old Murk-Eye had first driven the keeper's family from the lighthouse, then led the attack that killed them after they returned. Grayson wanted a scale as proof that the murloc behind those raids had been stopped.",["pending"]="{actor} would seek Old Murk-Eye and return a scale to Grayson.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought Old Murk-Eye's scale to Captain Grayson.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="52426014bd50b6208676b7cd382f95adb4cd71bc511255b403a9f9c8b8f19983",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[105]={["aftermath"]="Derrington confirmed the lich's defeat as a victory for the Horde.",["atomIDs"]={"105:description:1-85","105:description:90-173","105:description:176-328","105:description:331-410","105:description:415-482","105:objective:1-94"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"105:completion:1-15","105:completion:17-23","105:completion:25-53","105:completion:58-119","105:completion:121-201","105:completion:203-315"},["opening"]="Derrington's preparations had reached the lich at Andorhal's center. Araj's surrounding Scourge and formidable personal guard made the phylactery shard a dangerous proof to demand.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to confront Araj and bring back a shard.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the shard to Derrington.",["sourceHash"]="93bd2bff3b235b4a3e8356fc862ce7e7c5d80a4d0720185307b403dfd5802984",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[107]={["aftermath"]="William sympathized with the lovers, but still needed to work out how he could help.",["atomIDs"]={"107:description:1-64","107:description:69-100","107:description:103-152","107:objective:1-48"},["bridge"]="Gramma Stonefield's plan reached beyond the feuding farms. William Pestle, staying at Goldshire's Lion's Pride Inn, might know a potion that could help Maybell and Tommy Joe meet.",["bridgeFrom"]=111,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"107:completion:1-65","107:completion:67-107","107:completion:112-157","107:completion:159-173"},["opening"]="Gramma Stonefield's plan reached beyond the feuding farms. William Pestle, staying at Goldshire's Lion's Pride Inn, might know a potion that could help Maybell and Tommy Joe meet.",["pending"]="{actor} would carry Gramma's note to William Pestle.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Gramma Stonefield's note to William.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="37c7efbca4acfb494affec51dbecf9bf30ab92b8a9eb2379c079a90a6d437fcc",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[110]={["aftermath"]="Pestlezugg's results strengthened the suspicion of malignant outside control. He described the creatures as changed into ravagers, while the identity of that power remained unknown.",["atomIDs"]={"110:description:1-76","110:description:78-126","110:description:129-235","110:description:240-364","110:description:367-401","110:objective:1-81"},["bridge"]="The Scrimshank search had returned to Fizzledowser. While he examined the gear and personal effects, Pestlezugg's pending insect analysis needed to be checked.",["bridgeFrom"]=10,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"110:completion:1-35","110:completion:38-48","110:completion:50-77","110:completion:82-182","110:completion:185-295","110:completion:298-346","110:completion:349-387"},["opening"]="Fizzledowser turned to Scrimshank's equipment and personal effects while waiting for answers about the insects. Pestlezugg's analysis needed checking, lest the loss be only the first of many.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to ask Pestlezugg about the insect-part analysis.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} checked with Alchemist Pestlezugg about his analysis.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="663114c7599e2bc5bbe1ce87f1fbcfe84eaa84185111deacc0f939f6e4b3df30",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[111]={["aftermath"]="Gramma thought a brief meeting might still be possible while the families continued to feud.",["atomIDs"]={"111:description:1-32","111:description:35-102","111:description:107-142","111:objective:1-29"},["bridge"]="Tommy Joe believed his grandmother could find a way around the quarrel separating him from Maybell. She waited in the house east of him, close to the family dispute that made their future uncertain.",["bridgeFrom"]=106,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"111:completion:1-89","111:completion:91-145","111:completion:150-170"},["opening"]="Tommy Joe believed his grandmother could find a way around the quarrel separating him from Maybell. She waited in the house east of him, close to the family dispute that made their future uncertain.",["pending"]="{actor} would speak with Gramma Stonefield about the two lovers.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} sought Gramma's help for Tommy Joe and Maybell.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="c9546ec2ac48fcfae6a5f0a54f1efa0c2f229c4c21620e9474d222ac63756282",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[113]={["aftermath"]="Fizzledowser accepted Pestlezugg's judgment that the findings should be shared freely. He set aside the Water Company's usual interest in selling information and prepared a copy.",["atomIDs"]={"113:description:1-66","113:description:69-79","113:description:81-127","113:description:130-262","113:description:265-363","113:description:368-464","113:description:466-502","113:objective:1-64","113:objective:67-147"},["bridge"]="The analysis was ready and alarmed Pestlezugg. He wanted Fizzledowser to read it immediately and copy it for a warning extending beyond Gadgetzan.",["bridgeFrom"]=110,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"113:completion:1-131","113:completion:136-323","113:completion:326-388","113:completion:391-432"},["opening"]="Pestlezugg regarded his findings as urgent news far beyond Gadgetzan. He feared a threat spreading across southern Kalimdor and perhaps Azeroth, and wanted the surveyor to duplicate the report for wider warning.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to deliver Pestlezugg's report to Fizzledowser and obtain its requested copy.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the report-and-copy exchange with Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="e3adcaf88fe30077acbfa587616aa04cc718d2096df92e61be066efc6db6571c",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[115]={["atomIDs"]={"115:description:1-145","115:description:148-286","115:description:291-362","115:description:365-451","115:objective:1-53"},["opening"]="Blackrock shadowcasters had brought midnight orbs into the fighting. Marris held these dark devices responsible for serious harm to Redridge's defenders and wanted three removed from circulation for destruction.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to recover three Midnight Orbs from Blackrock shadowcasters.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered three Midnight Orbs to Marris for disposal.",["sourceHash"]="5f1531b63834329e8399eea4e7c0fb7f7fb4e7300fe70f42520bd1693f08b00b",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[116]={["atomIDs"]={"116:description:1-40","116:description:43-79","116:description:82-123","116:description:126-156","116:description:161-194","116:description:199-406","116:description:409-469","116:objective:1-127"},["opening"]="The invasion had delayed Daniels' liquor shipment and left his bottles nearly dry. Restocking the Lakeshire bar required a circuit through Westfall, Stormwind, Darkshire and Goldshire for four different drinks.",["pending"]="{actor} would obtain the lager, Merlot, Moonshine and Sweet Rum for Daniels.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the requested Thunderbrew Lager, Merlot, Moonshine and Sweet Rum to Daniels.",["sourceHash"]="7f224694e08edaddb99a794c0e5a1893e21f5583e2228fc5ca9cfe4d1796530a",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[123]={["aftermath"]="Dughan had heard of the Collector but did not yet know who employed him.",["atomIDs"]={"123:description:1-172","123:description:177-283","123:description:288-309","123:description:312-363","123:objective:1-72"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"123:completion:7-78","123:completion:80-106","123:completion:108-142"},["opening"]="A schedule set out the days and times for collecting gold from Elwynn's mines. Its unnamed recipient appeared to live near Brackwell Pumpkin Patch, a lead important enough to put before Dughan.",["pending"]="{actor} would take the Collector's schedule to the marshal.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the schedule to Marshal Dughan.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="4dd8f1ed6ab83491057638b940f71d28977c4deb61f186b15477939e3063b31f",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[124]={["atomIDs"]={"124:description:1-40","124:description:43-158","124:description:163-237","124:objective:1-77"},["opening"]="Gnoll brutes and mystics stalked the ridge north of Osgood's stable and took horses that strayed too far. With orcs already threatening Lakeshire, the stablemaster needed help against this nearer danger.",["pending"]="{actor} would confront ten Redridge Brutes and eight Redridge Mystics for Osgood.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Osgood's assignment against ten Redridge Brutes and eight Redridge Mystics.",["sourceHash"]="a86c2ce9932972757f3481fea161a9699dc980bfea416c4dfbbb2bf95f5e26a8",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[125]={["atomIDs"]={"125:description:1-35","125:description:38-95","125:description:98-180","125:description:183-245","125:description:248-309","125:description:314-372","125:objective:1-95"},["opening"]="Oslow's tools had suffered two transport disasters: a broken bridge stopped the wagon, then an orc catapult sank the boat. The toolbox now lay on Lake Everstill's bottom while the besieged town waited for work to resume.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to recover Oslow's toolbox from Lake Everstill.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned the sunken toolbox to Foreman Oslow.",["sourceHash"]="e64f804f09b7999451d718359ea56f5d0d22ed757513386141371f5617986cec",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[126]={["atomIDs"]={"126:description:1-35","126:description:38-103","126:description:106-165","126:description:170-210","126:description:213-238","126:description:243-298","126:description:301-319","126:objective:1-49"},["opening"]="Osgood still heard gnolls baying in the hills above Lakeshire, with Yowler's cry carrying over the rest. He hoped the leader's death would scatter the pack and asked for a paw as proof.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to bring Yowler's Paw to Osgood.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Yowler's Paw to Verner Osgood.",["sourceHash"]="5370a89854c002a1c2795946e6ad1dd1b8fe3ccefab9806410844b726c4b4113",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[127]={["atomIDs"]={"127:description:1-49","127:description:52-104","127:description:109-161","127:description:164-237","127:objective:1-58"},["opening"]="Everstill's spotted sunfish commanded a steady market, and Dockmaster Baren was short of stock. He offered a bargain for ten fish, leaving their recovery to fishing or the murlocs that carried them.",["pending"]="{actor} would obtain ten Spotted Sunfish for Baren.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied Dockmaster Baren with ten Spotted Sunfish.",["sourceHash"]="a938ee35a83a2dd6efd4935085e98bbef276ebba9eea907e836dfad16f9bfe7f",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
