[171]={["atomIDs"]={"171:description:1-37","171:description:40-104","171:description:107-116","171:description:119-241","171:description:244-288","171:description:290-303","171:description:308-360","171:description:363-432","171:objective:1-138"},["opening"]="The child thanked the caretaker for a week unlike the sorrow that preceded it. Thoughts of becoming a hero accompanied the last request: return to the orphanage and tell the matron about their time together.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to return the Human Orphan Whistle to Nightingale.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned the Human Orphan Whistle to Orphan Matron Nightingale.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="c4eb706df456fa35dffa1fadca59ccf7386dc4e49f9fc65b10e19b1c2aa60518",["sourceMapID"]="?",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[172]={["atomIDs"]={"172:description:1-48","172:description:51-120","172:description:125-142","172:description:145-254","172:description:257-341","172:description:344-381","172:description:386-438","172:description:441-490","172:objective:1-102"},["opening"]="Battlewail welcomed help during Children's Week. A temporary whistle would let the volunteer meet and summon the child placed in their care.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to use the Orcish Orphan Whistle to meet the ward.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the introductory conversation with the orcish ward.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="4728bd0e35798c4c10c6a1e0c91a3afb5d20e54226d51cb26a19454b92fa1634",["sourceMapID"]="?",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[173]={["atomIDs"]={"173:description:46-104","173:description:234-304","173:description:306-365","173:description:370-488","173:objective:1-61"},["opening"]="Calor left the Night Watch for Master Carevin's campaign against evil. To test a new recruit, he pointed toward the Nightbane Shadow Weavers in Brightwood Grove and the Rotting Orchard; words of support would not satisfy him.",["pending"]="{actor} would undertake Calor's assignment against six Nightbane Shadow Weavers.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Calor's assignment against six Nightbane Shadow Weavers.",["sourceHash"]="5a1ea0ae215df1fc540b570c76dd87a71927a334ff5c32794f6913f57b441f1f",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[174]={["atomIDs"]={"174:description:1-104","174:description:107-194","174:description:199-251","174:description:254-306","174:objective:1-71"},["opening"]="Viktori Prism'Antras sought an explanation for Duskwood's transformation beyond magic. With Cog's help, he intended to build a device for looking at the stars; the blueprint began with an engineer's bronze tube.",["pending"]="{actor} would obtain a Bronze Tube for Viktori.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied Viktori with the Bronze Tube his device required.",["sourceHash"]="202ca4c9bed82859626791e012ed660326457bcbd7e73bd0d35f1b28ae88ca2a",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[175]={["atomIDs"]={"175:description:1-72","175:description:75-190","175:description:193-291","175:description:294-341","175:objective:1-83"},["opening"]="Cog's design next required a reflective surface. Viktori remembered Mary, once known for carrying a looking glass, and thought she lived in southern Duskwood.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to find Mary and inquire about a reflective surface for Viktori.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reached Blind Mary with Viktori's request.",["sourceHash"]="af8ab2dadf57e53db2c92123d594d6ed1aad716d1faf5b66ebf3374be4320399",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[177]={["atomIDs"]={"177:description:1-55","177:description:59-72","177:description:75-126","177:description:129-182","177:description:185-208","177:description:211-283","177:objective:1-94"},["opening"]="Mary discarded her treasured looking glass behind the barn after an incident she left unnamed. She suspected an Insane Ghoul picked it up; rumor placed the creature in Tranquil Gardens Cemetery.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to recover Blind Mary's Looking Glass for Viktori.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Blind Mary's Looking Glass from the Insane Ghoul to Viktori.",["sourceHash"]="1cc9dceccf85e6fcb82ea00d0db020c3cb5e015b666a55e8558c72bc758f0ca1",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[178]={["atomIDs"]={"178:description:1-33","178:description:58-116","178:description:119-232","178:description:237-319","178:description:322-379","178:description:384-443","178:objective:1-58"},["opening"]="A pendant carried a distant message from Theocritus of Tower Azora. The mage identified it as a means of communication between Shadowhide gnolls and Morganth; his research might finally had reached such a pendant, and he asked to examine it.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to bring the Faded Shadowhide Pendant to Theocritus.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Faded Shadowhide Pendant to Theocritus.",["sourceHash"]="d766277bc4110aa2efcf812189777bd0ff9f20b65ca78d25a95b9d23191cb157",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[180]={["atomIDs"]={"180:description:1-26","180:description:31-135","180:description:138-218","180:description:221-273","180:objective:1-83"},["opening"]="Lakeshire's warrant named Lieutenant Fangore as leader of the Shadowhide clan under Morganth. Solomon demanded his death, with the gnoll's paw to establish that the warrant had been carried out.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to bring Lieutenant Fangore's paw to Solomon after the assignment.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} fulfilled the warrant against Lieutenant Fangore and delivered his paw to Solomon.",["sourceHash"]="e74f5f5eaca6b6ce84b7414308f243520db9b8b6af55b04ba29bb22258270a11",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[181]={["aftermath"]="With the final lens available, Viktori pronounced the stargazing device complete. The long search for its parts gave way to the research he had intended it to serve.",["atomIDs"]={"181:description:1-63","181:description:66-111","181:description:114-198","181:description:203-290","181:description:293-360","181:objective:1-103"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"181:completion:1-8","181:completion:10-43","181:completion:45-58","181:completion:60-90"},["opening"]="One optical piece remained. Cog's blueprint needed a large lens, and Viktori knew of a suitably oversized monocle worn by Zzarc'Vul at the southern ogre mound.",["pending"]="{actor} would obtain Zzarc'Vul's monocle for Viktori's device.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought Zzarc'Vul's monocle to Viktori.",["sourceHash"]="5f5645f6dd5f26fb7d6bce898331d73a92e0b6c65cc2f7d83106842af2f4ea57",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[184]={["aftermath"]="Furlbrow hoped the deed would let his family reclaim their land if Westfall became safe for honest farmers again.",["atomIDs"]={"184:description:1-60","184:description:63-130","184:description:133-187","184:description:192-231","184:description:234-314","184:description:319-354","184:description:357-439","184:description:444-496","184:objective:1-41"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"184:completion:1-20","184:completion:22-156","184:completion:161-214"},["opening"]="The Furlbrows' stolen deed carried a note about coercion and forgery. It also placed the displaced couple beside a broken wagon, leaving a chance to restore the document before their claim to the farm disappeared with them.",["pending"]="{actor} would return the deed to Farmer Furlbrow.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} restored the deed to Farmer Furlbrow.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="b6b92553d78ed1cb670ce8ccb650786c8f79672da7db2a20fb12eee0117e8092",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[185]={["atomIDs"]={"185:description:1-78","185:description:83-142","185:description:145-186","185:description:189-245","185:description:250-323","185:objective:1-88"},["opening"]="Ajeck began her lessons where her father had begun hers: with tigers. The young cats near the expedition camp offered a first test of tracking as well as hunting.",["pending"]="{actor} would undertake Ajeck's assignment against ten Young Stranglethorn Tigers.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Ajeck's assignment against ten Young Stranglethorn Tigers.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="1227828b43733ca3ed83380bf39557dac4cfb0c7ec0b49fcb11948aa86756f2a",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[186]={["atomIDs"]={"186:description:1-21","186:description:24-72","186:description:74-116","186:objective:1-82"},["bridge"]="Ajeck's first test had returned to camp. She now moved from young tigers to ten mature cats, increasing the danger without separating the hunt from its tracking lesson.",["bridgeFrom"]=185,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="Ajeck moved the test from young cats to mature Stranglethorn tigers. The number remained ten, but the quarry marked a harder stage of her instruction.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to meet Ajeck's challenge against ten Stranglethorn Tigers.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} fulfilled the assignment against ten Stranglethorn Tigers.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="4adada6f9f738d9e484ed6244ff210943f8d3eea32ae5d29731d8debaeecd6bf",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[187]={["atomIDs"]={"187:description:1-64","187:description:67-121","187:description:124-261","187:description:266-370","187:objective:1-88"},["bridge"]="The mature-tiger assignment led to a harder measure. Ajeck wanted ten elders, the cats she considered fiercest and most difficult to locate, before offering a final challenge.",["bridgeFrom"]=186,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="Ajeck set the elder tigers as the last broad test before a final hunt. She considered them both the hardest to find and the fiercest to face, making ten of them a measure of more than persistence.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to undertake the challenge against ten Elder Stranglethorn Tigers.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the assignment against ten Elder Stranglethorn Tigers.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="a61bab442dbdc251c2de34e266819c4b0c9ba720461c0e93d809b8948906472d",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[188]={["aftermath"]="Ajeck accepted the proof as the completion of her tiger-hunting instruction and named the hunter a master of that quarry.",["atomIDs"]={"188:description:1-50","188:description:53-99","188:description:102-128","188:description:131-204","188:description:207-255","188:description:260-298","188:objective:1-91"},["bridge"]="The elder-tiger test had brought the lessons to one quarry. Sin'Dall had evaded weeks of tracking, and Ajeck now required her paw as proof of the final hunt.",["bridgeFrom"]=187,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"188:completion:1-26","188:completion:29-67"},["opening"]="Weeks of tracking had not brought Sin'Dall within the expedition's grasp. Ajeck's final challenge turned from numbers to one elusive tiger, with a paw demanded as proof.",["pending"]="{actor} would track Sin'Dall and bring her paw to Ajeck.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the Sin'Dall assignment and delivered her paw to Ajeck.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="275b9140dc3b2fac155dc2bfdd2b7867fa7f9ba64197571eb3c10077eca2f093",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[189]={["atomIDs"]={"189:description:1-12","189:description:14-63","189:description:65-138","189:description:140-163","189:description:165-206","189:description:211-228","189:description:230-244","189:description:246-314","189:description:316-327","189:description:329-334","189:description:347-372","189:description:374-397","189:description:402-419","189:description:421-501","189:objective:1-65"},["opening"]="Kebok counted lost guards and mounting costs from troll skirmishes in the jungle. Fearing what Revilgaz would make of the losses, he offered payment for fifteen Bloodscalp ears.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to gather fifteen Bloodscalp Ears for Kebok.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered fifteen Bloodscalp Ears to Kebok.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="a6aa939eb2bb1e6ce8cd3cdd3e796d5628a6ae008f605131e1b80f128f67fc52",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[190]={["atomIDs"]={"190:description:1-147","190:description:150-193","190:description:196-241","190:description:246-293","190:objective:1-6","190:objective:11-82"},["opening"]="Erlgadin made panther hunting a condition of joining Hemet's company. His opening test called for ten young panthers, with finding the cats already counted as half the difficulty.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to undertake Erlgadin's first panther challenge.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the assignment against ten Young Panthers.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="0d7a0cf7e1dcf528bb6c64fadd001424b0f2accb1159308b5d0949582e882b00",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[191]={["atomIDs"]={"191:description:1-39","191:description:42-186","191:description:191-217","191:description:220-282","191:objective:1-6","191:objective:11-76"},["opening"]="The next panthers were no longer young. Erlgadin raised the test to ten mature cats, linking acceptance among the big-game hunters to the ability to face tougher quarry.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to meet the challenge against ten Panthers.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} fulfilled Erlgadin's assignment against ten Panthers.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="c7450dc093ad9fb080b3b14b86e78df60b7556997e8191a5d3bd1286cbc96690",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[192]={["atomIDs"]={"192:description:1-18","192:description:21-120","192:description:123-171","192:description:176-250","192:objective:1-6","192:objective:11-86"},["opening"]="Erlgadin named Shadowmaws as Stranglethorn's deadliest panthers. Their difficulty in the fight matched their difficulty to track, and ten formed the next test.",["pending"]="{actor} would undertake the assignment against ten Shadowmaw Panthers.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the assignment against ten Shadowmaw Panthers.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="4146ead3514b2306ff2c1c592001c5db1a220f0cde108c661eeb139642f3503b",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[193]={["aftermath"]="Erlgadin acknowledged Bhag'thera's death and praised the result of the final panther test.",["atomIDs"]={"193:description:1-64","193:description:67-131","193:description:134-162","193:description:165-224","193:description:229-294","193:objective:1-6","193:objective:11-92"},["bridge"]="The Shadowmaw assignment had reached Erlgadin. His final test turned to Bhag'thera, the panther that still eluded the party, with a fang required to establish the result.",["bridgeFrom"]=192,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"193:completion:1-32","193:completion:34-51","193:completion:53-79"},["opening"]="Bhag'thera had eluded the expedition while prowling the jungle. Erlgadin's final request sought a fang from that great panther as the evidence that ordinary hunting tests could not supply.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to obtain the Fang of Bhag'thera for Erlgadin.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Fang of Bhag'thera to Sir S. J. Erlgadin.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="6ab13131644d2002ed84a4351154223b265d2b41fd74695693127326f485edbf",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[194]={["atomIDs"]={"194:description:1-54","194:description:57-94","194:description:97-156","194:description:159-211","194:description:216-264","194:description:267-308","194:objective:1-60"},["opening"]="Hemet began his own test with ten Stranglethorn raptors. He refused to reveal their location, treating the search itself as an essential part of a big-game hunter's work.",["pending"]="{actor} would seek out ten Stranglethorn Raptors for Hemet's challenge.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Hemet's assignment against ten Stranglethorn Raptors.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="4febd41fc7b8e45c54d23c015fb0511e548da66dd976c78e816e7e075329567a",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[195]={["atomIDs"]={"195:description:1-59","195:description:62-138","195:description:141-166","195:objective:1-55"},["opening"]="Hemet raised the raptor challenge to Lashtails. Another ten animals stood between the initial test and the more difficult hunting he had in mind.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to undertake Hemet's challenge against ten Lashtail Raptors.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} fulfilled the assignment against ten Lashtail Raptors.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="83c3e0bf2a51a5a95e16b34a4ec0dbd5880a6e69927d60eef2ffbb73bc797be0",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[196]={["atomIDs"]={"196:description:1-45","196:description:48-90","196:description:93-121","196:description:124-228","196:description:231-299","196:objective:1-54"},["opening"]="Jungle Stalkers offered Hemet a test of craftier quarry. He considered the breed harder to track and defeat than the earlier raptors, promising a greater hunt after ten of them.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to meet the Jungle Stalker challenge.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Hemet's assignment against ten Jungle Stalkers.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="46866c1cd052e345a47e147f842a6760c7b71ee6edb271f1bb0f8ba8c9311d61",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[197]={["aftermath"]="Hemet greeted the returning hunter as a master raptor slayer. The elusive quarry had supplied the result his earlier challenges were designed to test.",["atomIDs"]={"197:description:1-139","197:description:142-182","197:description:187-266","197:description:269-334","197:objective:1-89"},["bridge"]="The Jungle Stalker test had led to the hunt Hemet promised. Tethis remained a raptor even he had failed to kill, and its talon was the proof he wanted brought back.",["bridgeFrom"]=196,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"197:completion:1-29","197:completion:34-59"},["opening"]="Hemet admitted that even he had failed to bring down Tethis. The elusive raptor named by Ajeck became the final measure of mastery, with a talon required to establish the result.",["pending"]="{actor} would confront Tethis and return a talon to Hemet.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the Tethis assignment and returned to Hemet with the required proof.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="4016eaad99fb67f9cc905680b725f91ece982528e46462fdf290756a5c93c47d",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[198]={["atomIDs"]={"198:description:1-4","198:description:6-53","198:description:55-141","198:description:146-232","198:description:234-320","198:description:322-421","198:description:423-446","198:description:451-499","198:objective:1-61"},["opening"]="Troll attacks had delayed the northern rebels' regular supply delivery. Krazek entrusted the goblin goods to a carrier for Private Thorsen, either at Doren's camp near Duskwood or on patrol south of it.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to deliver the Miscellaneous Goblin Supplies to Thorsen.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Miscellaneous Goblin Supplies to Private Thorsen.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="4c1933ab7418d5bf6443a5556962872f0be29f4a8f844203fb10e182c9d82e2e",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[199]={["atomIDs"]={"199:description:1-49","199:objective:1-78"},["opening"]="A sample of strange-smelling powder was the clue taken from the suspicious site. Hinderweir needed to see it before anyone could judge what threatened the dam.",["pending"]="{actor} would show the powder sample to Chief Engineer Hinderweir.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned to Hinderweir with the strange-smelling powder.",["sourceHash"]="3799e347e4d89d39cbfd6d5f5f88245b5fe55c4464407fb664789fc856e9847c",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[200]={["atomIDs"]={"200:description:1-66","200:description:69-112","200:description:117-172","200:description:175-270","200:description:273-362","200:description:367-470","200:description:473-509","200:objective:1-28"},["bridge"]="Thorsen's explanation had reached Doren, leaving a dangerous question: who exposed the secret infiltration? Herod's records in Kurzen's compound offered the first place to trace the leak.",["bridgeFrom"]=215,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="Doren feared a spy had exposed Thorsen's secret work. Kurzen's logistics officer Herod kept records upstairs in the compound's two-story house; those papers might reveal how the infiltration had been discovered.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to find Bookie Herod's Records.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the search for Bookie Herod's Records.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="9d6ace0a44c51e98d5efaf6a4f130d433ee953ed8c61f08c1694d972b98f826e",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[201]={["aftermath"]="Krazek judged the hunters unlikely to interfere with his operation. His interest shifted toward selling them manufactured goods.",["atomIDs"]={"201:description:1-125","201:description:128-233","201:description:236-321","201:description:326-389","201:objective:1-70"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"201:completion:1-46","201:completion:48-59","201:completion:61-224","201:completion:226-232"},["opening"]="Reports of hunters upriver from the Venture Company mine caught Krazek's attention because Hemet Nesingwary was said to be among them. The hunter's connections made the camp worth locating.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to locate the hunters' camp and report its position to Krazek.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} found the hunters' camp and reported its location to Krazek.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="7b1e49aeb719de2058f4413db347580dbbd840a31c2fbaf38693cab349794f04",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[202]={["aftermath"]="Doren accepted the proof that Kurzen and his leaders were defeated. Other menaces remained in the jungle, but he no longer counted the colonel's cruel intellect among them.",["atomIDs"]={"202:description:1-109","202:description:112-211","202:description:216-266","202:description:269-355","202:description:360-372","202:description:375-419","202:objective:1-103"},["bridge"]="The special-forces assignment had brought its report to Doren. He now sought Kurzen himself and his remaining leaders deep in the Stockpile, placing the rebel band's hopes on that confrontation.",["bridgeFrom"]=574,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"202:completion:1-63","202:completion:65-100","202:completion:102-119","202:completion:124-218","202:completion:220-265"},["opening"]="Doren placed the rebel band's hopes in a strike deep inside the Stockpile. Kurzen commanded from the cave behind his defenders, and the assignment called for his elite troops, subchiefs and head.",["pending"]="{actor} would undertake the Stockpile assignment against Kurzen and his specified leaders.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the assignment against six Kurzen Elite and four Subchiefs, delivering Kurzen's Head to Doren.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="7fa63e9f0fd340678aa3f381147d8b52130a7ae139c8c962af55411209937083",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[203]={["atomIDs"]={"203:description:1-51","203:description:54-125","203:description:128-190","203:description:195-238","203:description:241-253","203:description:256-306","203:objective:1-31","203:objective:36-78"},["opening"]="Kurzen's force outnumbered Yohwa's rebels at least ten to one. The sergeant sought survival through the colonel's own covert methods: strike the eastern camp and withdraw before reinforcements closed.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to meet Yohwa's assignment against fifteen Kurzen Jungle Fighters.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the assignment against fifteen Kurzen Jungle Fighters and returned to Yohwa.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="62cd40543737027a0c1cbd950c17389dfb79656f964cca58dc8eade8e91fbc73",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[204]={["atomIDs"]={"204:description:1-73","204:description:76-212","204:description:217-264","204:description:267-427","204:objective:1-85"},["opening"]="Kurzen's medicine men supplied healing remedies and poisoned the rebels with fern extracts. Yohwa wanted both materials taken for his own people, weakening the colonel's medical advantage in the process.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to recover seven Jungle Remedies and one Venom Fern Extract.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered seven Jungle Remedies and a Venom Fern Extract to Sergeant Yohwa.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="995fbf6431ad0293d2f46dea55c552e947dfe26edec0fc6b3f3df28fd7c32aa6",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[205]={["aftermath"]="Nimetz planned to examine the fetishes for an explanation of Kurzen's fall. Possessing the objects had not yet established their part in it.",["atomIDs"]={"205:description:1-87","205:description:90-246","205:objective:1-67"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"205:completion:1-10","205:completion:13-99"},["opening"]="Nimetz continued studying the recovered legends while seeking more tangible evidence of troll magic. Skullsplitter witchdoctors and mystics in the distant south carried the fetishes he wanted to examine.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to bring four Skullsplitter Fetishes to Nimetz.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered four Skullsplitter Fetishes to Brother Nimetz.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="275be1eaf69a5c3de2a8ab29c19ed3f1281effc039934067a90fd9416db8d515",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[206]={["aftermath"]="Nimetz intended to study the Mind's Eye for a possible good use. If that failed, he believed destruction was the only acceptable fate for the artifact.",["atomIDs"]={"206:description:1-67","206:description:70-208","206:description:211-301","206:description:306-418","206:description:423-500","206:objective:1-57"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"206:completion:1-4","206:completion:6-20","206:completion:22-90","206:completion:95-164","206:completion:166-174","206:completion:176-201"},["opening"]="Nimetz believed the cause of Kurzen's corruption remained alive in the eastern mountains. Rumors of Mai'Zoth's mind-control magic had convinced him that the ogre mage and his Mind's Eye could produce another such fall.",["pending"]="{actor} would recover Mai'Zoth's Mind's Eye for Nimetz.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Mind's Eye to Brother Nimetz.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="91481e176e5c99c064c9d82f78615f344f21d19438e86206d85538a3dcb1dc77",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[207]={["aftermath"]="The transcribed legends gave Nimetz material to test a link between troll magic and Kurzen's corruption. His response preserved that inquiry as unfinished.",["atomIDs"]={"207:description:1-93","207:description:96-135","207:description:138-189","207:description:194-260","207:description:263-306","207:description:309-374","207:description:379-507","207:objective:1-66"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"207:completion:1-14","207:completion:16-137"},["opening"]="Nimetz could not reconcile Kurzen's former nobility with his present depravity. He suspected troll magic and sought transcriptions from four ancient tablets at Bal'lal, the Vile Reef and Zul'Kunda to test that theory.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to transcribe all four tablets for Nimetz.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the four tablet legends to Brother Nimetz.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="3de1044629ae83c72d0d49840b7b365ec3397cbd828e9dd7eac55a2a3e36129e",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[208]={["aftermath"]="Hemet welcomed the hunter as a comrade of the expedition. His recognition concerned hunting and tracking proved through the final assignment.",["atomIDs"]={"208:description:1-43","208:description:46-179","208:description:184-272","208:description:275-323","208:description:326-366","208:description:369-418","208:description:421-496","208:objective:1-90"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"208:completion:1-17","208:completion:19-26","208:completion:28-88","208:completion:93-163","208:completion:165-226","208:completion:231-251","208:completion:253-259"},["opening"]="The white tiger King Bangalash was the prize that had drawn Hemet into the jungle. Beyond the expedition's lesser tests, the great cat's head was the proof he wanted for its highest hunting challenge.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to bring King Bangalash's head to Hemet.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered King Bangalash's head to Hemet Nesingwary.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="07b4e77ff16d26c42ebf5e2bdecaf0472cb03756c179432beca22c4d4489e4d5",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[209]={["atomIDs"]={"209:description:1-116","209:description:118-245","209:description:250-333","209:description:338-425","209:description:427-504","209:objective:1-56"},["opening"]="Kebok's export trade had found a dishonest substitute for costly tiger fangs. Skullsplitter tusks could be fashioned into convincing forgeries, and eighteen were needed for the monthly shipment.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to obtain eighteen Skullsplitter Tusks for Kebok.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied Kebok with eighteen Skullsplitter Tusks.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="c86b8ed805c841bd598c815c5b9bff6d146c9ba8ce836f813ae6469e7d0d1d50",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[210]={["atomIDs"]={"210:description:1-37","210:description:40-148","210:description:151-170","210:description:173-217","210:description:222-285","210:description:288-306","210:objective:1-46"},["opening"]="Kaleb's mechanical pot had once saved hours in the rebel camp's kitchen. Now it was broken, and its Booty Bay seller Krazek was the person asked to repair it.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to carry Krazek's Crock Pot back for repair.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Krazek's Crock Pot to Krazek.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="26504aa9771b68723781987106ec0440a4e85d60720e14ea2b9307f1dd234da6",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[211]={["aftermath"]="Valorfist accepted Araj's defeat as a victory for the Alliance.",["atomIDs"]={"211:description:1-85","211:description:90-173","211:description:176-328","211:description:331-410","211:description:415-482","211:objective:1-99"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"211:completion:1-15","211:completion:17-23","211:completion:25-53","211:completion:58-122","211:completion:124-204","211:completion:206-321"},["opening"]="Valorfist directed the assault at the power ruling Andorhal rather than its outer defenses. The lich's phylactery, guarded amid the city's center, would provide proof that Araj had fallen.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to recover a phylactery shard for Valorfist.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought the shard to Chillwind.",["sourceHash"]="3b308f2f09727008a9faf4b355685bc2ac3d12d30285480cf91de755f1d00af1",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[212]={["atomIDs"]={"212:description:1-69","212:description:72-92","212:description:94-188","212:description:193-326","212:description:331-453","212:description:456-468","212:objective:1-106"},["opening"]="A noble's birthday left Angus with a dish that could not wait. Cold Eye basilisk meat spoiled quickly, so the haunch for his chilled specialty needed swift delivery from northwestern Stranglethorn.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to bring Angus a fresh Chilled Basilisk Haunch.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Chilled Basilisk Haunch to Angus Stern.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="8bf9c49c5fdc78fe186ceff6fa000d8efbc497c6293ff4dc8254420c96c7805f",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[213]={["atomIDs"]={"213:description:1-23","213:description:25-166","213:description:171-253","213:description:258-264","213:description:266-271","213:description:273-287","213:description:289-408","213:description:410-507","213:objective:1-66"},["opening"]="Kebok chose theft as his answer to Gelriz's encroachment on Revilgaz's interests. The Venture Company geologists near Lake Nazferiti were studying blue crystals, and eight samples would carry out that choice.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to recover eight Tumbled Crystals for Kebok.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered eight Tumbled Crystals to Kebok.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="b0003f9513adb281bcb9e42103a683b2899a6a30862426824a92caaa44436500",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[214]={["aftermath"]="Riell offered the People's Militia's salute. She placed the effort within a hoped-for return of the land to its people, rather than declaring that struggle finished.",["atomIDs"]={"214:description:1-75","214:description:78-176","214:description:181-268","214:description:271-353","214:description:356-449","214:description:452-465","214:objective:1-83"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"214:completion:1-14","214:completion:16-79","214:completion:81-160"},["opening"]="Riell had learned that the Defias bandanas' material signified rank. The highest members were expected in VanCleef's hideout, where ten silk examples could supply proof of a strike against the leadership.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to gather ten Red Silk Bandanas for Riell.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered ten Red Silk Bandanas to Scout Riell.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="70f43bf5b54b5c758782b86376fa7796b63868904cd0318dd81405429ba369ca",["sourceMapID"]="?",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[215]={["atomIDs"]={"215:description:1-28","215:description:31-79","215:description:84-228","215:description:231-313","215:description:316-360","215:description:365-419","215:description:422-465","215:objective:1-46"},["opening"]="Thorsen explained that Doren had ordered his apparent return to Kurzen's force as a secret infiltration. The attempt had failed, and the lieutenant needed to be consulted without the mission becoming common knowledge.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to speak privately with Lieutenant Doren.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Lieutenant Doren at the Rebel Camp.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="fbe14e337078fcb1e0c4ca59494548a785d84812ba8b79f9f42a3dfad039058c",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[217]={["atomIDs"]={"217:description:1-73","217:description:76-170","217:description:173-208","217:description:211-282","217:description:287-393","217:description:396-501","217:objective:1-138"},["opening"]="Rugelfuss's scouts believed Grawmug led the Loch's troggs. The chieftain was never without his elite guards, Gnasher and Brawler; the captain hoped removing all three would weaken the incursion.",["pending"]="{actor} would confront Grawmug, Gnasher and Brawler for Captain Rugelfuss.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the assignment against Grawmug and both named guards, then reported to Rugelfuss.",["sourceHash"]="74a02ef17462e061ddbbf2b6549aec433f1d18a78f65dc9bee14678584b15378",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[219]={["atomIDs"]={"219:description:1-33","219:description:38-44","219:description:46-54","219:description:60-126","219:description:129-153","219:description:155-213","219:description:215-249","219:description:252-276","219:description:281-318","219:description:320-328","219:description:330-351","219:objective:1-57"},["opening"]="Keeshan remembered his regiment being overwhelmed by orcs before a blow to the head left him unconscious. Badly hurt and captive in a cave, he needed protection to make the journey back to Redridge.",["pending"]="{actor} would protect Corporal Keeshan during his escape.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the protection assignment for Keeshan's return to Redridge.",["sourceHash"]="fc810b6cdaae526e0dd59d5bfdf655d5e267752ca86fb46c36e60f36c10090ed",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[220]={["atomIDs"]={"220:description:1-80","220:description:82-153","220:description:158-177","220:description:179-207","220:objective:1-65"},["opening"]="Brine sent the pure-water vial onward to Islen. One further task remained before the next totem, and the prepared water would be needed for it.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to take the Vial of Purest Water to Islen.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Vial of Purest Water to Islen Waterseer.",["sourceClassMask"]="64",["sourceHash"]="da46477e101391301a2ebaed674dc5610a33384cb1043f76ea93351f0e3ddcfe",["sourceMapID"]="?",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[221]={["atomIDs"]={"221:description:1-96","221:description:98-178","221:description:183-277","221:description:279-333","221:description:338-354","221:objective:1-60"},["opening"]="Calor believed the larger Dark Runners formed the bulk of the worgen presence. He had seen them overrunning the Rotting Orchard southwest of town and warned that they presented a harder challenge.",["pending"]="{actor} would confront twelve Nightbane Dark Runners for Calor.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} fulfilled the assignment against twelve Nightbane Dark Runners.",["sourceHash"]="2af5ab9b36a7b86ce99347c0af6f920f410e00eab4f0454774fb04871d32dc29",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[222]={["atomIDs"]={"222:description:123-239","222:description:241-313","222:description:318-380","222:objective:1-85"},["opening"]="Bonfires marked the caves and southern mine where the most dangerous Nightbane worgen had settled. Calor's next targets were the Vile Fangs and Tainted Ones, eight of each.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to take on Calor's assignment against the Vile Fangs and Tainted Ones.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the assignment against eight Nightbane Vile Fangs and eight Nightbane Tainted Ones.",["sourceHash"]="134508f7f2478e6ce3d1fa26219f7fa1376fa5fa508638373db6d6fe6a241880",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[223]={["atomIDs"]={"223:description:18-54","223:description:59-127","223:description:132-190","223:description:192-258","223:objective:1-39"},["opening"]="Calor put a message on faded parchment into the hands of his prospective ally. His hope of expanding Carevin's ranks now traveled with the note to the man directing their work.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to carry Calor's note to Jonathan Carevin.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Calor's note to Jonathan Carevin.",["sourceHash"]="ba6171713e8e0488d66172a7b91ba8dad46c5f34c308e00e3961c1ab777c9f5c",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[224]={["atomIDs"]={"224:description:1-32","224:description:35-156","224:description:159-201","224:description:204-263","224:description:266-308","224:description:313-394","224:description:397-469","224:objective:1-122"},["opening"]="Ironforge's soldiers were far from home while troggs tunneled into Loch Modan. At the southern tower, Cobbleflint needed an assault on their ordinary fighters and scouts to shore up the depleted defenses.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to take on ten Stonesplinter Troggs and ten Stonesplinter Scouts for Cobbleflint.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Cobbleflint's assignment against the troggs and scouts.",["sourceHash"]="25af1add7edc17ab4fcda47789626d341226e29fae63bff6b4290e17e6f02d74",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
